    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **260 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit in the owner creation endpoint.\n\n**Change** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n```java\nLocalDate today = LocalDate.now();\nlong ownersCreatedToday = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n    .filter(existing -> today.equals(existing.getRegistrationDate()))\n    .count();\nif (ownersCreatedToday >= 100) {\n    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);\n}\n```\n\nThe check counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the current date and returns **429 Too Many Requests** when that count is 100 or more. It runs after the basic field-validation checks (so malformed requests still get 400) and before the create proceeds.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 added two integration tests to `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`:\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` \u2014 100 owners registered today \u2192 next POST returns 429.\n- `createOwnerAllowedWhenDailyLimitNotReached` \u2014 99 owners registered today \u2192 next POST returns 201.\n\nNotes: seed data (`data.sql`) inserts owners without a `registration_date`, so nothing pre-counts toward \"today\"; and existing tests that save owners directly via the repository also leave `registrationDate` null, so they're unaffected by the new limit.",
